### ============================================================
###  INSTRUCTOR API — Online Learning Platform
###  Base URL : http://localhost:1935/instructor-api
###  Auth     : Bearer token — login as INSTRUCTOR first via POST /auth/login
###             then set: Authorization: Bearer <token>
### ============================================================

### ── MEDIA UPLOAD (Cloudinary) ────────────────────────────────

### [1] Upload a Media File
###     Accepts: images (JPEG/PNG/WEBP/GIF), videos (MP4/WEBM/OGG/MOV),
###              PDFs, Word docs (.doc/.docx), PowerPoint (.ppt/.pptx),
###              plain text (.txt). Max size: 200 MB per file.
###     Field name MUST be "file".
###     Returns a Cloudinary secure_url to use in course content.
###
###     How to use in VS Code REST Client:
###       Replace the < path below with your local file path.
###       The extension sends it as multipart/form-data automatically.
POST http://localhost:1935/instructor-api/media
Authorization: Bearer <token>
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----FormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------FormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="intro-lecture.mp4"
Content-Type: video/mp4

< ./sample-files/intro-lecture.mp4
------FormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--

###

### ── COURSES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [2] Create a New Course (basic — no chapters yet)
###     The instructor field is taken from the JWT; no need to pass it.
###     Use PATCH /instructor-api/course/chapters after creation
###     to add the full chapter + quiz structure.
POST http://localhost:1935/instructor-api/course
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "title": "Mastering Java — From Zero to Hero",
    "category": "Programming",
    "thumbnail": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/image/upload/olp_media/java-banner.png",
    "demoVideo": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/olp_media/java-demo.mp4",
    "price": 999,
    "content": "A comprehensive Java course covering OOP, Collections, Streams, and Spring Boot."
}

###

### [3] Create a Course with Full Chapter Structure
###     chapters[] holds the rich content: units (text/video/doc) + quiz per chapter.
###     unitCount is auto-calculated from units.length — you can omit it.
POST http://localhost:1935/instructor-api/course
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "title": "React.js Complete Bootcamp 2025",
    "category": "Web Development",
    "thumbnail": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/image/upload/olp_media/react-banner.png",
    "demoVideo": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/olp_media/react-demo.mp4",
    "price": 1499,
    "content": "Master React from hooks to advanced patterns with real projects.",
    "chapters": [
        {
            "title": "Getting Started with React",
            "units": [
                {
                    "title": "What is React and Why Use It?",
                    "textContent": "React is a declarative, component-based JavaScript library for building user interfaces. It was created by Facebook and is now maintained by Meta and the open-source community.",
                    "videoContent": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/olp_media/react-unit1.mp4",
                    "documentContent": ""
                },
                {
                    "title": "Setting Up the Development Environment",
                    "textContent": "We will use Vite to scaffold our React project. Run: npm create vite@latest my-app -- --template react",
                    "videoContent": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/olp_media/react-unit2.mp4",
                    "documentContent": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/raw/upload/olp_media/setup-guide.pdf"
                }
            ],
            "quiz": [
                {
                    "question": "Which company originally created React?",
                    "options": ["Google", "Meta (Facebook)", "Microsoft", "Twitter"],
                    "answerIndex": 1
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "React Hooks Deep Dive",
            "units": [
                {
                    "title": "useState and useEffect",
                    "textContent": "useState manages local component state. useEffect runs side effects like data fetching after render.",
                    "videoContent": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/olp_media/react-unit3.mp4",
                    "documentContent": ""
                }
            ],
            "quiz": [
                {
                    "question": "Which hook is used to run code after every render?",
                    "options": ["useState", "useContext", "useEffect", "useReducer"],
                    "answerIndex": 2
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}

###

### [4] Get All My Courses
###     Returns all courses created by the logged-in instructor.
GET http://localhost:1935/instructor-api/courses
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### [5] Update Course Metadata (title, category, thumbnail, demoVideo, price, content)
###     Only the owning instructor can update it.
###     courseId is required; all other fields are optional.
PUT http://localhost:1935/instructor-api/course
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "title": "Mastering Java — Complete Bootcamp 2025",
    "category": "Programming",
    "thumbnail": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/image/upload/olp_media/java-banner-v2.png",
    "demoVideo": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/olp_media/java-demo-v2.mp4",
    "price": 1199,
    "content": "A deep-dive into Java 21, Spring Boot 3, and Microservices architecture."
}

###

### [6] Update / Replace All Chapters for a Course
###     Replaces the entire chapters array in one call.
###     Use this from the course editor after the instructor finishes editing.
PATCH http://localhost:1935/instructor-api/course/chapters
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "chapters": [
        {
            "title": "Getting Started with Java",
            "units": [
                {
                    "title": "Introduction & JDK 21 Setup",
                    "textContent": "Download the JDK 21 LTS from https://adoptium.net and set JAVA_HOME in your environment variables.",
                    "videoContent": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/olp_media/java-unit1-v2.mp4",
                    "documentContent": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/raw/upload/olp_media/jdk-setup.pdf"
                },
                {
                    "title": "Hello World — Deep Dive",
                    "textContent": "Every Java program starts with a class. The main method is the entry point: public static void main(String[] args).",
                    "videoContent": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/olp_media/java-unit2-v2.mp4",
                    "documentContent": ""
                }
            ],
            "quiz": [
                {
                    "question": "Which method is the entry point of a Java application?",
                    "options": ["start()", "run()", "main()", "init()"],
                    "answerIndex": 2
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "OOP Fundamentals",
            "units": [
                {
                    "title": "Classes, Objects & Constructors",
                    "textContent": "A class is a blueprint; an object is an instance. Constructors initialise the object state when it is created.",
                    "videoContent": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/olp_media/java-unit3-v2.mp4",
                    "documentContent": ""
                },
                {
                    "title": "Inheritance and Polymorphism",
                    "textContent": "Inheritance lets a child class reuse parent behaviour. Polymorphism allows a parent reference to point to a child object.",
                    "videoContent": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/olp_media/java-unit4-v2.mp4",
                    "documentContent": ""
                }
            ],
            "quiz": [
                {
                    "question": "What keyword is used to inherit a class in Java?",
                    "options": ["implements", "extends", "inherits", "super"],
                    "answerIndex": 1
                },
                {
                    "question": "What is runtime polymorphism also called?",
                    "options": ["Method overloading", "Method overriding", "Abstraction", "Encapsulation"],
                    "answerIndex": 1
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}

###

### [7] Toggle Course Visibility (single unified route)
###     isCourseActive: false → deactivates (hidden from students)
###     isCourseActive: true  → activates (visible to students)
PATCH http://localhost:1935/instructor-api/courses/toggle-status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "isCourseActive": false
}

###

### [8] Activate a Course (same toggle-status route, true value)
PATCH http://localhost:1935/instructor-api/courses/toggle-status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "isCourseActive": true
}

###

### ── DOUBTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [9] Get All Student Doubts for My Courses
###     Returns doubts posted by students actively enrolled in any of
###     the logged-in instructor's courses (Dropped students excluded).
###     Includes: student info, course info, matched doubt, instructor reply,
###               peer answers, repliedBy, matchedStudent.
GET http://localhost:1935/instructor-api/doubts
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### [10] Reply to a Student Doubt
###      The instructor can only reply to doubts from their own courses.
###      The student must still be enrolled (not Dropped).
###      Sets status → "Answered", records repliedBy + repliedAt.
PATCH http://localhost:1935/instructor-api/doubts/684d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b/reply
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "reply": "Great question! In Java, polymorphism allows a parent-class reference to hold a child-class object. When you call an overridden method on that reference, the JVM resolves it at runtime — this is called dynamic dispatch. See Chapter 2, Unit 4 for a live code example."
}
